# Executable text must stay LF, whatever the checkout platform does.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without these rules git rewrites shell scripts to
# CRLF on checkout — and a CRLF shebang line can leave `#!/bin/sh` unresolvable, which
# presents as the hook or script silently not running rather than as an error anyone can
# read. (`scale-space-foundations/.githooks/post-commit` is CRLF today for exactly this
# reason; worth the same guard there.)
*.sh        text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Workflow files are read by the runner on Linux; keep them LF for the same reason.
*.yml       text eol=lf
